# Flag operations in bulk: one store over a large uid set, a bulk
# flag fetch, many small stores, an expunge of half the mailbox and a
# fetch of what is left. Flags belong to (user, message) now, so the
# mailbox built by bigcopy holds few distinct messages and this is no
# longer a test of flag storage at scale. It is still the only script
# that drives these code paths with more than a handful of messages,
# which is how it caught a duplicate-key insert and a store that
# reported OK for a failed transaction.
depends bigcopy
send 1
bf1 uid store 1:1000 +flags.silent (f0 f1 f2 f3 f4 f5 f6 f7 f8 f9)
receive 3
* FLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen f0 f1 f2 f3 f4 f5 f6 f7 f8 f9)
* OK [PERMANENTFLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen f0 f1 f2 f3 f4 f5 f6 f7 f8 f9 \*)] permanent flags
bf1 OK done
send 1
bf2 uid fetch 1:1000 flags
receive 1001
